# ✋ Welcome to the service agent python-fastapi

Some of the things this agent provides for you:

## Developer Experience
- uv (use `uv add <package>` to add a new package; `uv add --dev <package>` for dev deps)
- hot-reload
- auto-generation of OpenAPI documentation

## Code
- OpenAPI

## Every listener this agent generates verifies the hop's admission

There is no option, and no line of yours to get right. What uvicorn serves is
`codefly_hop_entry.py`, a module this agent writes and rewrites on every start:
it wraps your whole FastAPI app in the authority's verifier, ahead of every
router, and the optional `grpc.aio` server carries the same verifier as an
interceptor. Nothing in `src/` installs the admission, so no edit in `src/` — and
no deleted line — removes it. The verifier is `codefly_hop.Verifier` from the
Codefly authority client, built from the keys source the composition names
(`authority/endpoint`), the audience the authority knows the module by
(`CODEFLY__MODULE`) and the replay store each single-use admission is reserved
in (`hop/replay-connection`, through `codefly_hop.replaypg`). A generated
service refuses to start without those inputs, which is the refusal the hop
itself makes, and there is no template setting that removes the verifier or
turns it off.

`/health` and `/ready` on the HTTP listener, the gRPC health service, and a
browser's CORS preflight are the only things served unauthenticated: none of
them is a caller. Every other route — the scaffold's and yours — is admitted
against the method the hop signed for it (`"<VERB> <path>"` for REST, the full
procedure for gRPC and Connect), with its single-use nonce reserved for as long
as the handler runs. A gRPC procedure the server does not serve is admitted
before it is answered, so an unstamped caller is told nothing about which
procedures exist. A developer run (`CODEFLY__ENVIRONMENT=local`) relaxes one
thing and only because the verifier relaxes it there: the reservations live in
the process rather than in a store every replica shares.

The scaffold ships the tests that say so (`tests/hop/test_admission.py`): an
unstamped call is refused, a call the hop stamped is served, an admission is
single-use and bound to its own route, health is open, and the wrap is in this
agent's entry rather than in your source.

**A service created before this agent carried the admission has none of it**:
it serves every route to anything that can address its listener. `Init`, `Build`
and `Deploy` say so and carry on until 2027-02-01, and refuse from then.
Migrating is by hand and takes three files plus a `codefly sync service`; the
procedure, including why the readiness probe has to move off `/version`, is
`docs/hop-migration.md` in codefly-dev/service-python-fastapi.


